+## 29.1 The four classes
+
+Every push names its class (`TRADEAI_PUSH_CLASS`, default `review`) and a typed reason
+(`TRADEAI_PUSH_REASON`). `TRADEAI_REMOTE_PUSH_AUTHORIZED=1` (or an active guard `git-push` grant)
+is still required for `wip` and `review`, as AGENTS.md §0 rule 4 says.
+
+| class | what it is | reason | limit | GitHub CI it starts |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| `wip` | continuity push of an agent branch whose PR is a **proven draft** | `claim:<claim id>` | 1 per 15 min per branch, 32 per branch per 24 h; fast-forward only; refused unless PR state proves draft | `draft-quick-check` + `agent-governance` (~2 runner-min) |
+| `review` | push of a branch whose PR is, or is about to be, **ready for review** | `claim:<claim id>` | estimated CI runner-minutes: 300 per branch and 3000 per repository per rolling 24 h (75 per full-fleet push) | the full fleet (~60-80 runner-min) |
+| `train` | the host release service, `refs/heads/train/<TRADEAI_RELEASE_TRAIN_ID>` only | `train:<train id>` | section 28; the ReleaseCapability@v1 reservation | the train's qualifying checks |
+| `operator` | the operator's own push | `operator:<grant id>` of an active guard `git-push` grant | none beyond the grant | as pushed |
+
+The train class is present but this package does not wire the generic hook to a verified
+host-service ReleaseCapability reservation. It therefore refuses matching train requests with
+`TRAIN_AUTHORITY_UNPROVEN`, including requests carrying AUTHORIZED or a guard override.
+`TRADEAI_RELEASE_TRAIN_ID` and `train:<id>` identify a request only. A separately reviewed
+reservation bridge is required before the train checkout can use this class; do not enable it
+by setting another environment variable. The operator path remains a separate operator act.
+
+## 29.2 Rules
+
+- **Reasons are typed and validated.** `claim:<id>` must name a live claim on the claim board
+  (`scripts/agent_claim.py`, heartbeat within the stale window, not merged or released) whose
+  branch is the pushed branch. A free-text, missing or mismatched reason is refused.
+- **`TRADEAI_REMOTE_PUSH_OVERRIDE` is retired.** Under v2 it lifts nothing. Going over a budget
+  needs an operator guard `git-push` grant whose reason says "override", named by
+  `TRADEAI_PUSH_REASON=operator:<grant id>`. While v2 is in shadow the flag works as in
+  section 17, and each use is written to the ledger with a warning.
+- **Agents never push `main`, `master`, `train/*` or tags**, in any class (AGENTS.md §25.1;
+  section 28). Deleting a remote branch is operator-only (AGENTS.md §0 rule 6).
+- **A `wip` push never rewrites history** (non-fast-forward is refused), so a cloud agent or another
+  vendor that fetched the branch never loses work.
+- **Open continuity PRs as drafts** (`gh pr create --draft`). Mark the PR ready only when local
+  acceptance (section 5) is green. That one transition starts the full fleet. Section 7 still holds:
+  a red review push is fixed locally, then one corrective review push.
+- **Budget decisions and reservations are serialized.** One shared lock spans the enforcing
+  decision, local preflights and durable ledger reservation across every worktree. Refusals
+  consume no ledger budget. Unreadable ledger state or failed writes refuse enforcement.
+  A successful pre-push hook reserves budget before transport; a later network failure stays
+  charged until operator reconciliation. A reservation is not proof of remote acceptance.
+- **WIP requires proven draft state.** Missing PRs, disabled lookup, API failures and unknown
+  state refuse WIP; initial branch publication uses review class before a draft can be opened.
+- **Every decision is logged.** The hook appends one line per decision, allowed or refused, to
+  `$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/tradeai-push-ledger.v2.jsonl` (`TradeAIPushEvent@v2`:
+  time, mode, class, branch, SHA, reason, claim, v1 and v2 verdicts, estimated cost, PR state,
+  whether the override flag was set). It is local, append-only and never source-controlled.
+- **The rules are read from the operator's checkout.** The hook loads `scripts/lib/tradeai_push_budget.py`,
+  `AI_WORK_POLICY.md` and `AGENTS.md` from the checkout the hook lives in (`core.hooksPath`), never
+  from the branch being pushed.
+- **This is not cryptographic security**, exactly as section 17 says. Cloud agents push from hosts
+  without this hook. For them the controls are GitHub-side: draft PRs run only the quick checks,
+  superseded runs are cancelled, and only ready, green PRs are trained.
+
+## 29.3 How this meets the release train (section 28; AGENTS.md §25)
+
+    local commits (hourly)
+      → initial review-class publication → DRAFT PR             (draft-quick-check only; never queued by the train)
+      → ... more wip pushes ...
+      → local acceptance green
+      → mark READY (or review push)     (full fleet once)
+      → required checks exactly success on the head
+      → the train's next window freezes it, integrates train/<id>, merges the batch PR, releases
+
+The train refuses drafts, held, stacked and conflicting PRs, and any PR whose required checks are
+not exactly `success` on its head (`release_train_controller` `_pre_exclusion`; AGENTS.md §25.2).
+A draft's skipped checks therefore never qualify anything. Train pushes are class `train`. They are
+not counted against any agent budget (section 28).
+
+## 29.4 Ratification
+
+The operator ratifies this section with `APPROVE_AI_WORK_POLICY_PUSH_V2 <pr_number> <head_sha>` on
